node_modules/

# dist/ is COMMITTED, deliberately.
#
# This package is distributed by GitHub TAG, not through a registry, and npm has no build or
# publish step for a git dependency: it checks the tree out and reads package.json. Every entry
# point here — main, module, types, exports — lives under dist/, so ignoring it shipped a
# package whose every path pointed at a file that was not there.
#
# The alternative was a `prepare` script that builds on install, which drags vite, vitest and
# the ProseMirror chain into every consuming project on every install. Committing the artifact
# costs a noisy diff per release; the other costs minutes per install, per project, forever.
#
# The risk this takes on is dist drifting from src, which fails SILENTLY — a consumer deploys
# and serves old components. Two things hold it: `npm version` rebuilds into the release commit,
# and CI rebuilds and fails if the result differs from what is committed.
*.local
.DS_Store
